<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer shares jump on Medica offering.</title>
<headline>Sulzer shares jump on Medica offering.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in engineering group Sulzer AG were strongly sought in Swiss pre-bourse trade after the group said it would list its medical technology unit Medica on the stock market.</p>
<p>Sulzer registered shares gained 82 Swiss francs or 9.8 percent to 920 Swiss francs before bourse trading opened.</p>
<p>&quot;This was exactly the step that the market has long demanded,&quot; one trader said about the public offering.</p>
<p>Sulzer had been the focus of persistent speculation that it would spin off one of its four industrial divisions or Medica.</p>
</text>
